 Here we have $x^2$ and $y^2.$ If we use the difference of squares formula, $x^2 - y^2 = (x+y)(x-y).$ Using the definitions of $x$ and $y,$ this becomes $$(2001^{2*1002}-2001^{-2*1002})(2001^{1002}-2001^{-1002}).$$  We could stop here if the numbers ended in $0,$ but we really can't do much with those numbers. The good thing about seeing these numbers is that they contain $1002$ and $2001,$ both exponents of $2001$ one greater than the other. One factor of $2001$ cancels an equivalent factor of $\frac{1}{2001}$ and one factor of $2001^2$ cancels an equivalent factor of $\frac{1}{2001}.$  $$\begin{aligned} 2001^{2*1002}&=2001^{1002}(2001^{1002}) \\ &=2001^{1001}(2001^{1001})(2001^2) \\ &=(x+y)(2001) \end{aligned}$$</think> $$\begin{aligned}2001^{-2*1002} &=2001^{-1001}(2001^{-1001})(2001^{-2}) \\ &=\frac{1}{y}\frac{1}{x}\frac{1}{2001} \\ &=\frac{1}{(x-y)2001} \end{aligned}
